                "remarks": "Not closed: (1) Lambda reserved concurrency, because the account concurrency quota is 10 and AWS requires 10 unreserved; it is exposed as var.lambda_reserved_concurrency. (2) WAF, which is not supported on HTTP APIs. (3) The Config rules were confirmed to evaluate correctly against the deployed (compliant) resources after apply, but drift was not simulated live on running infrastructure the way scripts/gap-regression.py simulates it against a plan \u2014 that is a known gap in test depth, distinct from the Rego suite's tested regression. (4) The SNS topic has no subscriber configured; wiring an on-call subscription is an organizational step. The blocked PR run shows the CI-time gate refusing a regression; the Config rules are the runtime counterpart."
